==Strategy==
If owned, [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] are very good picks for this stage. The former can tank considerable punishment from the assortment of Angels, while the latter has high movement speed, allowing it to enter Archer's blindspot.

Ideally, you should focus your lineup on Rushers and speedy units with less than 400 range, as they will be able to slip into Archer's blindspot.

Research [[Cat Combo]]s, such as [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], help spammable units like Ramen Cat become even more effective. If you have slots to spare, bringing combos can certainly help.

Archer only appears upon base hit and the starting Gabriels don't pose much of a threat, meaning it is quite easy to stall them out. Once you reach the base, let the first Angelic Gory near your base to separate them from Archer. Once isolated, they can be bursted down and killed, leaving Archer with minimal support. Repeat for the second Angelic Gory and the stage is practically won.

====Recommended Units====
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: If you have his [[True Form]] unlocked, he will be very useful in staggering the Angelic Gories and dealing with them quickly. '''Do not use his normal or evolved forms.'''
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: A very good heavy-hitting option for picking off the Angels, provided you protect them with meatshields. With their Double Bounty talent unlocked, they can also help with money management.
*[[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]]: A decent option for DPS if you lack Courier. Being speedier than [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], she has a higher chance to contribute, but be careful of her high cost.
* [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: If owned, Cafeteria is an excellent pick for a rusher due to their [[Massive Damage|massive damage]] to Angels along with high speed.
*[[The Invisible Cat (Special Cat)|Groom Cat]]: Another seasonal exclusive, his massive damage to Angels can help with the initial Gories, provided you lure them near your base. Otherwise, he can be a bit too slow to contribute.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]: If Ramen isn't enough, Sanzo's Target Angel Talent can help in controlling the Gories, but this becomes pretty inconsistent with Archer on the field.

